{
  "README": [
    "Human judgement about CI failures. Ground truth for the triage evals.",
    "",
    "This is the one artifact here that cannot be regenerated. captures/raw/ and",
    "captures/logs/ come from GitHub; meta.json is a projection of those. These",
    "labels exist only because Pavel wrote them, so they are edited by hand and",
    "never rewritten by a script.",
    "",
    "symptom: what CI showed. Extracted from logs; no judgement.",
    "cause:   why it happened. Pavel.",
    "fix:     the action actually taken or to take. Pavel. Categories get derived",
    "         from this field, so it must be the real next action.",
    "notes:   disagreements, uncertainty, anything that qualifies the above.",
    "",
    "One entry per incident. Labels apply to every run in runIds. If runs within an",
    "incident fail for different reasons, split into entries with disjoint runIds.",
    "status: unlabelled | labelled | unknown (Pavel could not reconstruct it).",
    "",
    "Bootstrapped 2026-09-15 from captures/; hand-maintained from then on."
  ],
